# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` for local Cloudflare development.
# NEVER commit the real values — `.env` and `.dev.vars` are gitignored.
#
# In production these are set as Cloudflare Pages secrets, not as files:
#   Workers & Pages -> your project -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OpenAI API key. Server-side only: it is read by the Pages Function in
# `functions/api/agent.ts` and must never reach the browser bundle. Note it is
# deliberately NOT prefixed with VITE_, since anything VITE_-prefixed is inlined
# into the client build and would be publicly readable.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional. Defaults to gpt-5.
#
# CONFIRM THIS AGAINST YOUR OWN ACCOUNT before the first deploy — which model
# ids you can call depends on your account and tier, and a 404 here silently
# drops the agent into its offline fallback. `openai.models.list()` or the
# dashboard will tell you what you have. Any tool-calling chat model works;
# a smaller one is a fine cost trade for this workload.
# AGENT_MODEL=gpt-4.1
